# Waveshare USB-TO-LoRa-HF candidate StratoPi flight configuration (100,000 ft).
# Design assumption: up to 500 km drift; this is not a wind prediction.
# Range-focused engineering starting point, not a validated flight link.
# Use permitted power/antenna settings for the exact dongle's US authorization.
# Applied to the dongle selected by PORT in .env. Run on each host separately.
# Commands run from top to bottom. Blank lines and # comments are ignored.
# These active setters CHANGE settings. Comment them out for inspection only.
# All lines are validated before opening the serial port.
# Firmware Ver1.2 supports the queries below. Each setter is followed by a
# readback that must match. The script pauses one second between commands.

# Enter command mode; AT+VER must follow immediately to confirm entry.
+++
AT+VER
AT+HELP

# Record current channel and spreading factor before changing settings.
AT+TXCH?
AT+RXCH?
AT+SF?

# Keep 915 MHz and 500 kHz bandwidth for the existing US fixed-channel plan.
AT+TXCH=65
AT+TXCH?
AT+RXCH=65
AT+RXCH?
# Keep SF10: messages worked at SF10 but failed at SF12 in hardware tests.
# Shorter airtime than SF12, at the cost of reduced weak-signal sensitivity.
AT+SF=10
AT+SF?
AT+BW=2
AT+BW?
# CR1 (4/5) -> CR2 (4/6): more error-correction redundancy; extra airtime.
AT+CR=2
AT+CR?

# Restore 18 -> 22 dBm (about 158 mW): +4 dB power; higher battery demand.
# This is the module maximum, not a claim of approval for every antenna/setup.
AT+PWR=22
AT+PWR?
AT+MODE=1
AT+MODE?
AT+NETID=42
AT+NETID?
AT+ADDR=479
AT+ADDR?
# Keep LBT enabled to reduce collisions; it can defer transmission, not ensure delivery.
AT+LBT=1
AT+LBT?
# Keep RSSI bytes off until the text receiver can parse them.
AT+RSSI=0
AT+RSSI?

# CRC is already enabled in the firmware; no CRC command is needed.
# Setters must return OK/+OK. Errors, timeouts, and echo-only AT replies fail.
# The +++ entry command may return only its echo; AT+VER confirms entry next.
# Save accepted changes and return to transparent mode.
AT+EXIT
